---
import {
	HOMELAB_REPOSITORY_URL,
	SITE_TITLE,
} from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
	'Infrastructure projects by Stephen McCruden, including a reproducible Kubernetes homelab and automated GitOps delivery pipeline.';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Projects | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description}>
	<main id="main-content" class="page">
		<header class="page-hero">
			<div class="page-hero-copy">
				<p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>
				<h1>Infrastructure projects with the implementation left visible.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					My projects are built to show how a system is provisioned,
					configured, operated, and recovered—not only what it looks
					like when everything is healthy.
				</p>
			</div>
			<aside class="page-hero-aside">
				<p>Project standard</p>
				<p>
					Version-controlled configuration, documented decisions,
					repeatable validation, and an explicit failure path.
				</p>
			</aside>
		</header>

		<section class="section" aria-labelledby="homelab-title">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Flagship project</p>
					<h2 id="homelab-title">Reproducible Kubernetes homelab</h2>
					<p>
						A three-node Proxmox environment used to practice the
						full platform lifecycle: infrastructure as code, Linux
						configuration, Kubernetes operations, GitOps, and
						observability.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<article class="feature-project">
				<div>
					<p class="project-kicker">Platform engineering</p>
					<h3>Built to be destroyed and rebuilt with confidence.</h3>
					<p class="project-summary">
						Terraform defines the virtual infrastructure. Ansible
						creates a consistent Fedora baseline and bootstraps the
						cluster. Flux owns the desired Kubernetes state. The
						result is an environment where the rebuild process is a
						maintained capability rather than an emergency document.
					</p>
					<ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Homelab technologies">
						<li class="tag">Proxmox</li>
						<li class="tag">Fedora Linux</li>
						<li class="tag">Terraform</li>
						<li class="tag">Ansible</li>
						<li class="tag">Kubernetes</li>
						<li class="tag">Cilium</li>
						<li class="tag">Flux</li>
						<li class="tag">SOPS</li>
					</ul>
					<div class="button-row">
						<a
							class="button button-primary"
							href={HOMELAB_REPOSITORY_URL}
							target="_blank"
							rel="noreferrer"
						>
							View the repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
						</a>
						<a class="button button-secondary" href="/blog">
							Read project notes
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<dl class="fact-list">
					<div>
						<dt>Physical layer</dt>
						<dd>3-node Proxmox cluster</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Compute layer</dt>
						<dd>Fedora Kubernetes nodes</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Delivery model</dt>
						<dd>Infrastructure as code and GitOps</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Operations</dt>
						<dd>Metrics, runbooks, and failure testing</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section class="section" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Delivery architecture</p>
					<h2 id="architecture-title">Each tool has a clear responsibility.</h2>
					<p>
						Keeping ownership boundaries explicit makes the rebuild
						path easier to reason about and failures easier to isolate.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="numbered-grid">
				<article>
					<span>01 / Provision</span>
					<h3>Terraform</h3>
					<p>
						Defines virtual machines, compute, storage, network
						settings, and placement across Proxmox.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span>02 / Configure</span>
					<h3>Ansible</h3>
					<p>
						Builds the Fedora baseline, configures containerd, and
						applies repeatable system hardening.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span>03 / Reconcile</span>
					<h3>Flux</h3>
					<p>
						Continuously applies controllers, shared configuration,
						and applications from Git.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span>04 / Observe</span>
					<h3>Prometheus</h3>
					<p>
						Surfaces cluster and workload behavior through metrics,
						dashboards, and health signals.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section" aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">What the project demonstrates</p>
					<h2 id="outcomes-title">Operational outcomes, not a tool inventory.</h2>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="card-grid">
				<article class="card">
					<span class="card-number">01</span>
					<h3>Repeatable rebuilds</h3>
					<p>
						The cluster lifecycle is expressed in code and procedures
						instead of relying on undocumented manual steps.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="card">
					<span class="card-number">02</span>
					<h3>Visible system behavior</h3>
					<p>
						Telemetry and verification make health and failure states
						inspectable before decisions are made.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="card">
					<span class="card-number">03</span>
					<h3>Tested recovery paths</h3>
					<p>
						Node failures, application rollouts, and restore
						assumptions are treated as engineering work.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section split-section" aria-labelledby="site-title">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Application delivery</p>
				<h2 id="site-title">This portfolio runs on the platform.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="body-copy">
				<p>
					Astro produces a static site, GitHub Actions publishes an
					unprivileged container to GHCR, and Flux automatically
					promotes immutable image digests into separate preview and
					production Kubernetes workloads.
				</p>
				<p>
					The pipeline gives the site the same review, rollback, and
					audit trail expected from the rest of the infrastructure.
				</p>
				<div class="pipeline" aria-label="Website delivery pipeline">
					<span>Markdown</span>
					<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
					<span>Astro</span>
					<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
					<span>GHCR</span>
					<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
					<span>Flux</span>
					<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
					<span>Kubernetes</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section split-section" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Technology</p>
				<h2 id="stack-title">Current platform stack.</h2>
			</div>
			<dl class="stack-table">
				<div>
					<dt>Compute</dt>
					<dd>Proxmox · Fedora Linux</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Automation</dt>
					<dd>Terraform · Ansible · Python</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Platform</dt>
					<dd>Kubernetes · Cilium · Flux</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Traffic</dt>
					<dd>Traefik · cert-manager · Cloudflare</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Visibility</dt>
					<dd>Prometheus · Grafana</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Delivery</dt>
					<dd>GitHub Actions · GHCR · SOPS</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</section>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
